  "epilogue": [
    "By midnight, the House of Culture was empty except for police, federation officials and the unfinished final pairings. The brass bell sat in an evidence bag on Boris’s desk, beside the cold coffee and the blank result slip.",
    "The federation suspended the Bitola Open’s results while it reviewed the Round Eight records. Maja Velkova refused the provisional title until every score was checked, and the players agreed to return the following month for a clean final round.",
    "Sara Dinevska received her arbiter’s certificate the next winter. She kept Boris’s green desk lamp in the club office and used it whenever someone asked her to correct a result without a written reason.",
    "The tournament now begins with two bells: one for the players, and one for the record. The second bell is never rung unless every clock, score sheet and signature agrees."
